Description: xf86CheckSlot: scfb, like an autoconfigured fbdev, must be the only device.
 With no xorg.conf, autoconfiguration on FreeBSD lists modesetting and then
 scfb as the platform's fallback framebuffer driver (xf86AutoConfig.c,
 listPossibleVideoDrivers). modesetting claims the KMS device on the
 platform bus; scfb then claims the console framebuffer with
 xf86ClaimFbSlot(), and xf86CheckSlot() let it: it treats an autoconfigured
 Linux fbdev as incompatible with any other device, but for scfb it only
 compares DRI paths, which scfb has none of. The result was a second X
 screen (:0.1) on the same display:
   (II) Matched scfb as autoconfigured driver 1
   (II) scfb(1): using default device
 scfb always drives the console's framebuffer (vt(4)'s efifb/vbefb, or a
 boot framebuffer), which is the display a KMS driver already drives, so it
 gets fbdev's rule both ways: a candidate scfb device is refused when any
 other device is claimed, and nothing is claimed after an scfb device.
 Without KMS nothing else is claimed and scfb drives the display as before.
 X.Org's server had the same effect through platformSlotClaimed and
 pciSlotClaimed in xf86ClaimFbSlot(), which XLibre replaced with
 xf86CheckSlot().
Origin: NextBSD
 (nextbsd/nextbsd-xlibre#22, item 4)
Forwarded: not yet; a candidate for X11Libre (xf86CheckSlot on FreeBSD)
---
--- a/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Bus.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Bus.c
@@ -720,6 +720,15 @@
                 fbPath = "";
             }
         }
+        else
+        if (!strcasecmp(fb_ptr->driver, "scfb")) {
+   /*
+    * scfb (FreeBSD, DragonFly) always drives the console's framebuffer,
+    * which is the display a KMS driver already drives: like an
+    * autoconfigured fbdev device, it must be the only device.
+    */
+            fbPath = "";
+        }
     }
 
    /*
@@ -781,7 +790,8 @@
 #endif
 
         if (pent->bus.type == BUS_NONE) {
-            if (!strcasecmp(pent->driver->driverName, "fbdev")) {
+            if (!strcasecmp(pent->driver->driverName, "fbdev") ||
+                !strcasecmp(pent->driver->driverName, "scfb")) {
                 if ((type != BUS_NONE) || (fbPath == NULL)) {
                     /* fbdev without busID is incompatible with other types */
                     LogMessageVerb(X_INFO, 1,
